  // (93% DRAM throughput) and its theoretical occupancy (66.7%) is limited
  // by its 64 registers/thread. Replace the CuTe global-memory tensors --
  // whose 64-bit stride state stays live in registers across the whole
  // kernel -- with lean 32-bit precomputed strides plus raw per-batch base
  // pointers, so the compiler can fit more CTAs per SM (together with the
  // higher launch-bounds CTA target) and keep more DRAM requests in
  // flight. CuTe is retained for the shared-memory staging layout.
